NAME
       exit, _exit, exit_group - terminate a process

SYNOPSIS
       #include <unistd.h>

       void _exit(int status);
       void exit(int status);

DESCRIPTION
       Ends the calling process with STATUS, of which the low eight
       bits reach the parent through wait. exit runs the registered
       atexit handlers and flushes stdio first; _exit does neither.

       exit_group ends every task in the group, which is how a process
       that has spawned helpers tears them all down at once.

       On exit the kernel closes the file table, hands any children to
       init, releases the terminal's non-blocking mode if this process
       had set it, and stops the audio stream if this process had
       opened it. Nothing else has to be cleaned up by hand.

RETURN VALUE
       Does not return.

SEE ALSO
       wait(2), fork(2), kill(2)
